      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you encounter a situation where the battery casing is punctured and the device starts smoking or getting hot, it's crucial to act quickly and safely to suppress the lithium fire. Here's the standard procedure:\n\n1. Immediately power down the device by holding the power button until it shuts off.\n2. Remove the battery if it is user-replaceable. If not, do not attempt to remove it yourself.\n3. Place the device in a safe, non-conductive container to prevent any accidental short circuits.\n4. Do not attempt to extinguish the fire with water, as this can cause a chemical reaction and worsen the situation.\n5. If the fire is small and manageable, you can use a Class D fire extinguisher, which is specifically designed for metal fires, including lithium fires. Aim the extinguisher at the base of the fire and sweep side to side.\n6. If the fire is large or spreading, evacuate the area immediately and call emergency services for assistance.\n7. Do not attempt to move the device or the container until the fire is completely extinguished and you are sure it is safe to do so.\n8. Once the fire is out, contact your local waste management service for guidance on how to dispose of the",
